 "summary": "Raises the minimum supported GCC version from 12.1 to 13.1, enforcing support via a CMake check for C++20 `std::format`. It updates CI environments to GCC 13/Ubuntu 24.04, drops active NetBSD cross-compilation from GitHub Actions while updating its environment scripts to GCC 14, and refactors several idioms to use standard C++20 constructs (`std::format`, `std::type_identity`, structured bindings capture in lambdas, and folding expressions).",
 "problem": "Supporting GCC 12 prevents adopting standard C++20 features such as `std::format`, requires custom workarounds like `ALWAYS_FALSE` for static assertions in dependent contexts, and blocks future transitions toward C++23.",
